            <ArticleTitle>Posterior femoral cutaneous neuralgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1146-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A middle-aged male developed a right posterior femoral cutaneous neuralgia that persisted for 10 years without any associated neurologic, electrophysiologic, or radiologic findings. Five years after onset, surgical exploration of the subgluteal area identified a venous malformation surrounding the nerve. The syndrome appears unique and exemplifies all major aspects of the sensory distribution of the nerve complex.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
